"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,610\nThe Learning Brain. Series 8: Assessment That Teaches\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,416\nEpisode 11\n\n3\n00:00:07,496 --> 00:00:10,256\nIntegrity in the age of AI\n\n4\n00:00:13,056 --> 00:00:16,417\nGenerative AI can write an essay in seconds.\n\n5\n00:00:16,743 --> 00:00:20,387\nMany instructors have turned to AI detectors to catch it.\n\n6\n00:00:20,769 --> 00:00:23,010\nBut how fair are those detectors?\n\n7\n00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:26,131\nIn 2023, Weixin Liang,\n\n8\n00:00:26,504 --> 00:00:33,880\nJames Zou and colleagues at Stanford tested seven widely used AI detectors on essays written by people.\n\n9\n00:00:34,527 --> 00:00:38,243\nThey used ninety one essays by non native English speakers,\n\n10\n00:00:38,551 --> 00:00:40,222\nwritten for the TOEFL exam,\n\n11\n00:00:40,498 --> 00:00:43,660\nand eighty eight essays by American eighth graders.\n\n12\n00:00:43,830 --> 00:00:47,601\nThe detectors were nearly perfect on the American students' essays.\n\n13\n00:00:48,009 --> 00:00:54,853\nBut on average they flagged sixty one percent of the non native speakers' essays as AI generated.\n\n14\n00:00:55,447 --> 00:00:59,348\nAlmost ninety eight percent were flagged by at least one detector.\n\n15\n00:00:59,518 --> 00:01:00,069\nWhy?\n\n16\n00:01:00,238 --> 00:01:02,874\nDetectors look for predictable word choices.\n\n17\n00:01:03,239 --> 00:01:07,536\nWriters with a smaller vocabulary in English write more predictably,\n\n18\n00:01:07,764 --> 00:01:10,167\nso their human writing looks machine like.\n\n19\n00:01:10,337 --> 00:01:18,962\nAnd the same study showed that a simple prompt asking AI to vary its word choice could get AI written text past the detectors.\n\n20\n00:01:19,371 --> 00:01:23,585\nSo detectors can both accuse the innocent and miss the guilty.\n\n21\n00:01:23,755 --> 00:01:26,560\nThat shifts attention from detection to design.\n\n22\n00:01:27,137 --> 00:01:29,267\nAssignments that include drafts,\n\n23\n00:01:29,365 --> 00:01:31,576\nprocess notes, in class writing,\n\n24\n00:01:31,793 --> 00:01:38,924\noral explanations, or reflections on personal experience make it easier to see students' own thinking.\n\n25\n00:01:39,094 --> 00:01:42,984\nThis connects to Series three: decide where AI can help,\n\n26\n00:01:43,004 --> 00:01:46,375\nsay so clearly, and assess the thinking you care about.\n\n27\n00:01:46,545 --> 00:01:47,373\nFor teaching.\n\n28\n00:01:47,674 --> 00:01:50,968\nDon't rely on a detector score as evidence on its own.\n\n29\n00:01:51,296 --> 00:01:54,216\nState your AI policy for each assignment.\n\n30\n00:01:54,665 --> 00:01:56,493\nBuild in visible process: outlines,\n\n31\n00:01:56,682 --> 00:01:59,791\ndrafts, conversations about the work.\n\n32\n00:02:00,227 --> 00:02:02,104\nOne tip to share with students: show your process,\n\n33\n00:02:02,305 --> 00:02:04,600\nnot just the product.\n\n34\n00:02:04,770 --> 00:02:09,318\nThe best protection for integrity is an assignment where the thinking shows.\n\n"